message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "When Does Geometry Beat a Token-Entropy Baseline for Predicting Semantic Entropy? A Robustness Audit of Training-Free Hallucination Signals"
abstract: >-
  Training-free geometric features of transformer hidden states have been proposed as
  cheap, probe-free signals of semantic uncertainty for hallucination detection. This
  work audits whether they deliver rather than proposing a detector, and finds that a
  trivial token-entropy baseline matches or beats every one of them, and that which
  features appear reliable is set by the evaluation split rather than by the geometry.
